.TH DENON\-REMOTE 1 "September 2026" "denon-remote 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
denon\-remote \- desktop remote control for Denon and Marantz receivers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B denon\-remote
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B denon\-remote
controls a Denon or Marantz network receiver over the local network.
.PP
It holds a single connection to the receiver on TCP port 23. That connection
carries both the commands the application sends and the notifications the
receiver emits on its own, so the window stays in step with changes made from
the front panel, the infrared remote or the HEOS app.
.PP
The list of inputs is read from the receiver rather than assumed: the labels
shown are the ones configured on the receiver, and inputs hidden in its setup
are left out. Receivers too old to report the list over that connection are
asked once for their web page on port 80 instead.
.SH USAGE
On first start the application scans the local network and offers the
receivers it finds; an address can also be typed in directly. The chosen
receiver is remembered, and the connection is re-established automatically
if it drops.
.PP
The window is divided into four tabs:
.TP
.B Main zone
Input, volume in decibels, mute and power.
.TP
.B Zone 2, Zone 3
The same controls for the other zones, plus the option to follow the main zone.
The zone 3 tab is shown only when the receiver has a third zone.
.TP
.B Sound
Surround modes, Quick Select presets under the names set on the receiver
(a fifth on models that have one), bass, treble and subwoofer trim, dynamic
range compression, Restorer, ECO mode and the sleep timer.
.TP
.B Menu
Cursor keys for the receiver's on-screen setup menu.
.PP
When a system tray is available, the application offers power, standby and
mute from its tray icon, and the mouse wheel over the icon changes the volume
by half a decibel per notch. The application can be told to close to the tray
instead of quitting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/denon-remote/denon-remote.conf
Stores the receiver address, the window geometry and the tray preference.
.SH NOTES
Bass and treble are ignored by the receiver unless tone control is enabled,
which is why those sliders are disabled until it is.
.PP
The receiver accepts only one control connection at a time on some firmware
versions. If the application cannot connect, check that no other controller
is holding the port.
.SH AUTHOR
mskpluk <mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>
